{"api_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/jax-ml/jax/issues/11895","collected_at":"2026-09-27T21:56:14.028306+00:00","comments":[{"author_association":"MEMBER","body":"> This can cause loud and confusing errors down the line\r\n\r\nArguably a separate issue to file regarding this: if we do somehow end up with unexpected 64-bit device (or abstract) arrays, we ideally catch that and err early on, ahead of lowering in particular.","created_at":"2022-08-13T00:10:58Z","html_url":"https://github.com/jax-ml/jax/issues/11895#issuecomment-1213604801","id":1213604801,"issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/jax-ml/jax/issues/11895","minimized":null,"node_id":"IC_kwDOCTkjjc5IViPB","performed_via_github_app":null,"pin":null,"reactions":{"+1":0,"-1":0,"confused":0,"eyes":0,"heart":0,"hooray":0,"laugh":0,"rocket":0,"total_count":0,"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/jax-ml/jax/issues/comments/1213604801/reactions"},"updated_at":"2022-08-13T00:10:58Z","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/jax-ml/jax/issues/comments/1213604801","user":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/123903?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/froystig/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/froystig/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/froystig/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/froystig/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/froystig","id":123903,"login":"froystig","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjEyMzkwMw==","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/froystig/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/froystig/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/froystig/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/froystig/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/froystig/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/froystig","user_view_type":"public"}},{"author_association":"NONE","body":"Reviving this issue.\r\n\r\nHi, I had experienced the same exact problem and the error I got was:\r\n```python\r\nXlaRuntimeError: UNKNOWN: <unknown>:0: error: type of return operand 0 ('tensor<1xi64>') doesn't match function result type ('tensor<1xi32>') in function @main\r\n<unknown>:0: note: see current operation: \"func.return\"(%0) : (tensor<1xi64>) -> ()\r\n<unknown>:0: note: in bytecode version 0 produced by: MLIR16.0.0git\r\n```\r\nWhich wasn't very intuitive to figure out. Furthermore, it seems that some tensorflow_datasets may use int64 to describe labels (like in tfds.load('mnist')) and if used together with dlpack it will result in this issue.\r\n\r\nIsn´t there a way to protect users from this, like a more intuitive RuntimeError, Warning?\r\n\r\nFor context I will leave [here the colab](https://colab.research.google.com/drive/1dXdlgdduOQ9SY_MIahMtpOZk1E5WcmLb?usp=sharing) that I used to replicate this issue.","created_at":"2022-10-11T13:03:15Z","html_url":"https://github.com/jax-ml/jax/issues/11895#issuecomment-1274655563","id":1274655563,"issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/jax-ml/jax/issues/11895","minimized":null,"node_id":"IC_kwDOCTkjjc5L-bNL","performed_via_github_app":null,"pin":null,"reactions":{"+1":0,"-1":0,"confused":0,"eyes":0,"heart":0,"hooray":0,"laugh":0,"rocket":0,"total_count":0,"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/jax-ml/jax/issues/comments/1274655563/reactions"},"updated_at":"2022-10-11T13:03:15Z","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/jax-ml/jax/issues/comments/1274655563","user":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/19167453?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/T-Almeida/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/T-Almeida/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/T-Almeida/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/T-Almeida/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/T-Almeida","id":19167453,"login":"T-Almeida","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE5MTY3NDUz","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/T-Almeida/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/T-Almeida/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/T-Almeida/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/T-Almeida/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/T-Almeida/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/T-Almeida","user_view_type":"public"}},{"author_association":"MEMBER","body":"@hawkinsp @jakevdp – So long as the x64 flag exists and means what it means, how should we behave on `jax.dlpack.from_dlpack` given a 64-bit-dtyped array, when x64 mode is off? Some options:\r\n\r\n1. Error\r\n2. Convert to 32-bit silently\r\n3. Convert to 32-bit and `warnings.warn`\r\n\r\nI'll send a PR for what we think is best.","created_at":"2022-10-20T18:34:23Z","html_url":"https://github.com/jax-ml/jax/issues/11895#issuecomment-1285977758","id":1285977758,"issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/jax-ml/jax/issues/11895","minimized":null,"node_id":"IC_kwDOCTkjjc5Mpnae","performed_via_github_app":null,"pin":null,"reactions":{"+1":0,"-1":0,"confused":0,"eyes":0,"heart":0,"hooray":0,"laugh":0,"rocket":0,"total_count":0,"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/jax-ml/jax/issues/comments/1285977758/reactions"},"updated_at":"2022-10-20T18:34:23Z","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/jax-ml/jax/issues/comments/1285977758","user":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/123903?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/froystig/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/froystig/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/froystig/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/froystig/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/froystig","id":123903,"login":"froystig","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjEyMzkwMw==","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/froystig/orgs","r